{:edb/db-before-t 827 :edb/db-after-t 828 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534140 50 #inst "2026-10-06T04:22:03.297Z" 13194139534140 true] [17592186087656 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278439 13194139534140 true] [17592186087656 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278446 13194139534140 true] [17592186087656 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278451 13194139534140 true] [17592186087657 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278425 13194139534140 true] [17592186087657 1020 #edb/ref 17592186278432 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278426 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1089 "q-107478" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1100 "Express $z=\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}}$ in the form $r(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).$" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1113 #uuid "663d89fa-6933-5875-9f60-94f2abd7d111" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278425 1145 "First, we express the given complex number in the form $z=x+y\\text{i}.$ To do this, we remove $\\text{i}$ from the denominator by multiplying the numerator and denominator of $z$ by the complex conjugate of the denominator, which is $1+\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{4}{1-\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{(1-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{{1}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1+\\text{i})}{1+1} \\\\  & =2(1+\\text{i}) \\\\  & =2+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn polar form, $r$ represents the magnitude $|z|.$ For a complex number $z=x+y\\text{i},$ the magnitude of $z$ is given by\n\n$$\n|z|=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nSo, for $z=2+2\\text{i},$ the magnitude is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nIn polar form, $\\theta $  represents the argument $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z).$ Since $x=2$ and $y=2$ are both positive, $z$ lies in the first quadrant. So, we can find $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the complex number $z$ in polar form:\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))\n$$" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278427 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278428 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278429 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278430 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278431 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1041 "selection" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278431 13194139534140 true] [17592186278426 1110 #uuid "e16ee0ba-b5a8-5f88-8376-d08aee32e493" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278427 1034 "z=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}))" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534140 true] [17592186278427 1111 #uuid "a3ab40e4-681d-5fb5-a137-e0d3f1769ce6" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278428 1034 "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534140 true] [17592186278428 1111 #uuid "0343d9f1-8adc-5264-8457-700aa44c4475" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278429 1034 "z=2\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}))" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278429 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534140 true] [17592186278429 1111 #uuid "acf51d53-ebcf-50fc-9117-ce6f5d3dabaa" 13194139534140 true] [17592186278430 1034 "z=\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\